atars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-19T16:14:54-07:00","id":868869,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/868712-obligatory-lunars-thread?p=868851#post868851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The <i>threads</i> stood for something.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh! Sorry, mis-read.<br /> Also: fair enough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-19T18:08:13-07:00","id":868945,"title":"","content":"Hopefully we are going to be getting WoD-style open playtests for the upcoming splats, if only so that I can get to playing out my age old Lunar concepts, top of which is my Sloth totem one named Bodhisattva of Endless Thought who has &quot;while hanging upside down from a tree&quot; as a specialty in all of his Social and Mental attributes.<br /> <br /> Squeeee!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10762-asoral","name":"Asoral","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10762_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-19T18:09:23-07:00","id":868947,"title":"","content":"I am so excited for Lunars. SO excited. We've been throwing stuff back and forth lately and it's all so fantastic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<span style=\"color:#5C5C5C\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">. ... for me, the transformative power of art is you are </span></span></span><i>not </i><span style=\"color:#5C5C5C\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">above the material.&quot; -= Guillermo del Toro</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9752-lucy-darling","name":"Lucy Darling","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9752_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"143"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-19T18:42:08-07:00","id":868972,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lucy Darling</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/868712-obligatory-lunars-thread?p=868947#post868947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am so excited for Lunars. SO excited. We've been throwing stuff back and forth lately and it's all so fantastic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Help this hoary old elder drum up some excitement:<br /> <br /> Has there been any official news about the Lunars in the last several months? I just stopped coming here when I couldn't finish any homebrew properly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-19T19:48:26-07:00","id":869023,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/868712-obligatory-lunars-thread?p=868972#post868972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Help this hoary old elder drum up some excitement:<br /> <br /> Has there been any official news about the Lunars in the last several months? I just stopped coming here when I couldn't finish any homebrew properly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nothing official I don't think - not counting corebook stuff. The release schedule is floating around somewhere but I am pretty sure Exigents are up next after DBs so Lunars are a little way off. <br /> <br /> I threatened John with a bearshark Lunar, unofficially. I'm also reading up on my mythology and we're having interesting discussions about how my Australian-ness intersects with mythology given my exposure to a narrative cosmology very unlike most others in the world, and one that is not a collection of myths as much as a current and thriving spiritual connection with the world. Unofficially.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<span style=\"color:#5C5C5C\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">. ... for me, the transformative power of art is you are </span></span></span><i>not </i><span style=\"color:#5C5C5C\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">above the material.&quot; -= Guillermo del Toro</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9752-lucy-darling","name":"Lucy Darling","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9752_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"143"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-19T20:16:43-07:00","id":869048,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lucy Darling</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/868712-obligatory-lunars-thread?p=869023#post869023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I threatened John with a bearshark Lunar, unofficially.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel compelled to provide a visual aid. <br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://nedroid.com/imagesb/bearshark2.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10291-zeesun","name":"Zeesun","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"252"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-19T20:30:50-07:00","id":869053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lucy Darling</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/868712-obligatory-lunars-thread?p=869023#post869023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nothing official I don't think - not counting corebook stuff. The release schedule is floating around somewhere but I am pretty sure Exigents are up next after DBs so Lunars are a little way off.<br /> <br /> I threatened John with a bearshark Lunar, unofficially. I'm also reading up on my mythology and we're having interesting discussions about how my Australian-ness intersects with mythology given my exposure to a narrative cosmology very unlike most others in the world, and one that is not a collection of myths as much as a current and thriving spiritual connection with the world. Unofficially.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I'd enjoy hearing more about Australian mythology, if you have some time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-19T21:17:06-07:00","id":869085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/868712-obligatory-lunars-thread?p=869053#post869053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think I'd enjoy hearing more about Australian mythology, if you have some time.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I guess the major difference (to things like Greek mythology or Egyptian or whatever) is that it is an active belief system for many Aboriginal people and there are some really complex aspects of who is allowed to know what, and who is given what bits of knowledge. Mother-in-law language is common, and it is evident in spiritual practice. How knowledge is transmitted is key as well - yarning is important culturally and is beginning to be the foundation of some new sociological movements which is great (I work at a university with a large research and support unit focused on Aboriginal people and research into Australian history).<br /> <br /> One of the things we talked about was the way that a lot of yarns have what feels like a fatalistic end. I was reading a kid's story once and excerpted it for them because it's about Aboriginal culture, and culture in general, but there's a small section talking about dances and what they mean. So there are dances about animals, right? The main character is talking to the white kids about what the dances mean. Except the dance for crocodiles is 'this kid didn't listen to the elders talk about where crocs are living and he got himself eaten because he was greedy', and the one about bees is 'holy shit white men's bees will kill you, run'. Absolutely vital lessons to be shared across the incredible number of linguistic and tribal lines of Australia, but they don't tend to have the same kinds of 'happy endings' or triumphs modern audiences expect (no pretty Narcissus turning into a flower for his sins, we have the Daughters running away to the sky to escape a terrible man). Which is because they aren't myths, reworked and retold and codified through centuries and millennia away from the living culture that created them, but are part of living culture now.<br /> <br /> When you grow up reading these stories and hearing these songs and watching these dances, while also getting folklore that talks about this weird frozen water from the sky at Christmas, or winter being a dead season (hell, winter as a season at all for half the country), it affects how you understand myths. <br /> <br /> The invasion of Australia is recorded in dances and yarns and so on, just like centuries of meteorological data, medical knowledge, things like that. So my experience of 'myth' is with a much more actively living thing than a lot of people outside Australia. Hell, even inside Australia - I didn't grow up on country or anything like that, but there are some nebulous connections around the place, and also I grew up in less white enclaves. And like I said, as an adult I have the advantage of some top level researchers to hang with.<br /> <br /> Also means I know how seriously terrible it would be to lift, say, the Quinkins and use them in a game. It's less about the stories themselves, and more about how they intersect with cultures. Like it's almost impossible to talk about Aboriginal culture because it isn't a culture, a language, or even series of dialects. Aboriginal mobs are as disparate as countries, obviously, given how big the country is. There are commonalities - connection to country, some common stories, some cultural stuff like eye contact, physical contact, conversation flow, but mostly it is tied to specific places and mobs. I'm no expert, I try and sit and listen when Aboriginal people speak, and this is some of what I've learned.<br /> <br /> In US terms Aboriginal culture is much more like First People's than anything else, and from what I can tell it takes a bigger part of modern Australian culture than First People in the US though.<br /> <br /> (note: I am a white woman, I grew up regional and in the country, but I'm a city dweller now)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<span style=\"color:#5C5C5C\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">. ... for me, the transformative power of art is you are </span></span></span><i>not </i><span style=\"color:#5C5C5C\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">above the material.&quot; -= Guillermo del Toro</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9752-lucy-darling","name":"Lucy Darling","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9752_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"143"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-19T23:41:05-07:00","id":869140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/868712-obligatory-lunars-thread?p=868720#post868720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Although I can't help but wonder: if 9-Tailed Mole-Hounds are natural creatures, maybe Orca-wolf and Sharktopus could be as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exalted's biology folks, where this could be accurate:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://s-media-cache-ak0.pinimg.com/236x/6a/da/11/6ada11c4dd562e0d98d585b04e497b3d.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">https://s-media-cache-ak0.pinimg.com...b04e497b3d.jpg</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3505,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","user":"Matt the Bruins fan","date":". 04-20-2016, 04:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-20T00:11:14-07:00","id":869151,"title":"","content":"Well, that's more something that happens in the Wyld.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-20T05:40:11-07:00","id":869245,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/868712-obligatory-lunars-thread?p=869140#post869140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Exalted's biology folks , where this could be accurate:<br /> <br /> [ATTACH=CONFIG]temp_562_1461134435077_955[/ATTACH]<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The image is a broken link for me :S","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-20T06:13:38-07:00","id":869260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/868712-obligatory-lunars-thread?p=869245#post869245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The image is a broken link for me :S</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, the forum software doesn't work so great with attachments.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-20T08:24:36-07:00","id":869332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lucy Darling</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/868712-obligatory-lunars-thread?p=869085#post869085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I guess the major difference (to things like Greek mythology or Egyptian or whatever) is that it is an active belief system for many Aboriginal people and there are some really complex aspects of who is allowed to know what, and who is given what bits of knowledge. Mother-in-law language is common, and it is evident in spiritual practice. How knowledge is transmitted is key as well - yarning is important culturally and is beginning to be the foundation of some new sociological movements which is great (I work at a university with a large research and support unit focused on Aboriginal people and research into Australian history).<br /> <br /> One of the things we talked about was the way that a lot of yarns have what feels like a fatalistic end. I was reading a kid's story once and excerpted it for them because it's about Aboriginal culture, and culture in general, but there's a small section talking about dances and what they mean. So there are dances about animals, right? The main character is talking to the white kids about what the dances mean. Except the dance for crocodiles is 'this kid didn't listen to the elders talk about where crocs are living and he got himself eaten because he was greedy', and the one about bees is 'holy shit white men's bees will kill you, run'. Absolutely vital lessons to be shared across the incredible number of linguistic and tribal lines of Australia, but they don't tend to have the same kinds of 'happy endings' or triumphs modern audiences expect (no pretty Narcissus turning into a flower for his sins, we have the Daughters running away to the sky to escape a terrible man). Which is because they aren't myths, reworked and retold and codified through centuries and millennia away from the living culture that created them, but are part of living culture now.<br /> <br /> When you grow up reading these stories and hearing these songs and watching these dances, while also getting folklore that talks about this weird frozen water from the sky at Christmas, or winter being a dead season (hell, winter as a season at all for half the country), it affects how you understand myths.<br /> <br /> The invasion of Australia is recorded in dances and yarns and so on, just like centuries of meteorological data, medical knowledge, things like that. So my experience of 'myth' is with a much more actively living thing than a lot of people outside Australia. Hell, even inside Australia - I didn't grow up on country or anything like that, but there are some nebulous connections around the place, and also I grew up in less white enclaves. And like I said, as an adult I have the advantage of some top level researchers to hang with.<br /> <br /> Also means I know how seriously terrible it would be to lift, say, the Quinkins and use them in a game. It's less about the stories themselves, and more about how they intersect with cultures. Like it's almost impossible to talk about Aboriginal culture because it isn't a culture, a language, or even series of dialects. Aboriginal mobs are as disparate as countries, obviously, given how big the country is. There are commonalities - connection to country, some common stories, some cultural stuff like eye contact, physical contact, conversation flow, but mostly it is tied to specific places and mobs. I'm no expert, I try and sit and listen when Aboriginal people speak, and this is some of what I've learned.<br /> <br /> In US terms Aboriginal culture is much more like First People's than anything else, and from what I can tell it takes a bigger part of modern Australian culture than First People in the US though.<br /> <br /> (note: I am a white woman, I grew up regional and in the country, but I'm a city dweller now)</div> </div> </div> </div>Very cool. Thank you. That perspective makes a bunch of stuff about societies that haven't developed portable written media make sense. I'd heard some similar things crop up when you look back into the origins of fairy tales and things, where most of them are really just there to tell you stuff like &quot;Seriously, DON'T get too close to the fire, people totes died doing that!&quot; or &quot;Look, arranged marriages might be depressing, but just try to get to know each other,&quot; but we've prettied them up and turned them from catchy parables about fire safety or not talking to strangers into complex narratives with endings that make us feel better about things, even if it destroys the real meaning of the story.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}